    "The development hereby permitted shall be commenced before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.<br>",
    "<p>The development hereby approved shall only be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:</p><ul><li>Planning Statement (received: 18/01/2024)</li><li>Design and Access Statement (dated: November 2023)</li><li>Existing and Proposed Side Elevations (drawing number: G1-03, revision 0, dated: November 2023)</li><li>Proposed Site Plan (drawing number: 409-GL-SP-102, revision P01, dated: 19/07/2017)</li><li>Site Location Plan (dated: 24/11/2023)</li><li>Proposed Front Elevations (drawing number: G1-03, revision 1, dated: March 2024)&nbsp;</li><li>Proposed Floor Plans (drawing number: G1-01, revision 1, dated: March 2024)&nbsp;</li><li>Refuse and Waste Strategy (recieved 15/03/2024)</li></ul><p>No other drawings or documents apply.</p>",
    "<p class=\"MsoNormal\">The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing dwellinghouse.<br></p>",
    "For the lifetime of the development, the proposal must function in accordance with the Refuse and Waste Strategy (Recieved: 15/03/2024) submitted and to the satisfaction of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "a)\tPrior to occupation details of all cycle storage including the design, quantum and location shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. All cycle storage shall be designed in accordance with the London Cycle Design Standards.&nbsp;b) The approved cycle storage shall be implemented and thereafter maintained for the lifetime of the development.&nbsp;"
